    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's an interesting way to put it. so u are saying that the act of staying to benefit from the system is the real indicator of failure? it feels like once you define it that way, the \"pragmatism\" argument kind of falls apart because it's just a way to rationalize being complicit. do you think most historians today actually view it as a moral failure rather than a political necessity?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
