      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, in most modern, critical historical analysis, the *choice to benefit from the system after its moral decline is the most damning evidence of complicity, not the initial political environment on its own.*\n\nThis perspective often views \"pragmatism\" in this context not as a political tool, but as a moral one, focusing on the active choice to prioritize self-preservation over ethical opposition.\n\nTherefore, the strong trend in current serious historical scholarship leans heavily toward framing these later-stage decisions as moral failings, even if the initial political leanings were more nuanced.",
      "source": "target",
